3.1 Selection rationale

TENTORA was selected because it connects discovery with execution. It does not stop at inspiration, profile browsing, template selection, or AI generation. It gives users a path to a usable output and preserves continuity between self-service and professional creative work.

4. Problem Definition

4.1 Core problem

Project owners frequently need creative work but lack a fast, clear, and visually understandable route to the right result.

The current process may require users to:

browse large numbers of unrelated creative profiles;

move between several disconnected platforms;

understand specialist design terminology;

compare creatives without a consistent framework;

coordinate multiple specialists independently; and

manage files, feedback, revisions, approvals, and delivery through separate tools.

4.2 Multi-service complexity

A restaurant or café may require brand identity, menus, packaging, social-media assets, advertising, digital displays, websites, motion graphics, staff products, and artwork. Finding and coordinating separate creatives can consume time and produce an inconsistent visual outcome.

4.3 Different users require different journeys

Client need

