7. Product Experience

7.1 Experience principles

Show before asking. Users should see sectors, services, templates, and creative work before completing forms.

Use plain language. Visual examples should explain services without requiring design terminology.

Minimize early input. Budget, deadline, and technical details are requested only when necessary.

Preserve continuity. A user can move from a template to a creative without re-entering existing information.

Keep choices focused. Recommendations remain curated rather than endless.

