8.5 Ready Design definition

A Ready Design is a structured creative system rather than a flat image. Depending on its service and license, editable properties may include:

text and content;

typefaces and type scale;

colors and brand tokens;

images and illustrations;

approved layout options;

motion speed and behavior;

format, dimensions, and output channel; and

logo and brand-asset placement.

8.6 Creator-led marketplace model

Ready Designs are primarily uploaded by approved creatives or studios. TENTORA provides curation, quality standards, structured editability, discovery, licensing, purchase, and creator attribution.

Every listed design must identify:

the original creative or studio;

editable and locked properties;

pricing and creator compensation;

permitted AI-assisted actions;

included output formats; and

the applicable commercial license.

TENTORA may also publish clearly identified collaborations or commissioned collections, but it must not present independent creative work as internally authored.

8.7 AI-assisted customization

Subject to creator permission and design rules, AI may:

reflow layouts according to content length;

suggest colors compatible with an uploaded logo;

remove image backgrounds;

improve product images;

generate missing visual elements when permitted;

adapt approved designs across channels;

translate or rewrite content;

create consistent variations; and

check readability, spacing, hierarchy, and visual balance.

8.8 Professional handoff

When deeper customization is required, the client can transfer the current work to the original creative or another suitable professional.

The handoff may include the selected template, client content, uploaded assets, saved edits, visual preferences, previews, and an AI-generated structured brief.

